<!doctype html>
<!--
  Template. Do not edit www/dist/index.html by hand.
  Double-brace tokens come from repo-root plus-pricing.json via www/build.mjs.
  An unsubstituted token is a build failure.

  Copy rules for this page:
  - The hero shows NO markdown syntax. No [[wikilinks]], no HTML comments, no
    frontmatter. Syntax is earned later, once someone knows what this is.
  - One running example (Sam and the apartment) carries the whole page.
  - Claims discipline: Ask search is literal keyword and tag matching, not
    semantic. Writes from chat are queued. Resurfacing only happens with the
    app open. Never soften any of those.
-->
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Atoms · Notes you can ask</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Atoms turns the notes you already take in Obsidian into something you can ask. Your words stay exactly as you wrote them."
    />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark light" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Atoms · Notes you can ask" />
    <meta
      property="og:description"
      content="You wrote it down. Atoms helps you find it again."
    />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://tryatoms.app" />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://tryatoms.app/og.png" />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="https://tryatoms.app/og.png" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://tryatoms.app" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <!-- Hero: understandable in three seconds, no syntax anywhere -->
      <header class="hero">
        <div class="wrap">
          <p class="eyebrow">Atoms · An Obsidian plugin</p>
          <h1>You wrote it down.<br />You never found it again.</h1>
          <p class="lead">
            Atoms turns the notes you already take into something you can ask.
          </p>

          <div class="chat">
            <p class="chat-line chat-line--you">
              what did Sam say about the apartment?
            </p>
            <div class="chat-line chat-line--them">
              <p class="chat-from">
                From <em>Sam regrets the building with no elevator</em> · March 4
              </p>
              <p class="chat-quote">
                sam says the building has no elevator and he regrets it
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="actions">
            <a class="btn btn--primary" href="#install">Get Atoms</a>
            <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="#how">See How It Works</a>
          </div>
          <p class="note">Free with your own Anthropic key.</p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <!-- The turn -->
      <section class="band">
        <div class="wrap">
          <p class="claim">
            A note you cannot find again is a note you did not take.
          </p>
          <p>
            Capture was never the hard part. You have years of it. Atoms is
            built for the other half.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- How it works -->
      <section class="band" id="how">
        <div class="wrap">
          <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
          <h2>You only do the first step.</h2>

          <ol class="steps">
            <li>
              <span class="sentinel" aria-hidden="true">↳</span>
              <div>
                <h3>Catch it in five seconds</h3>
                <p>
                  Atoms installs a shortcut on your iPhone. Run it from your
                  home screen, the share sheet, or Siri, and say the thought out
                  loud instead of typing it. It lands in today's daily note
                  before you have put your phone down.
                </p>
                <p>
                  On a desktop, type a line. Either way, nothing new to learn
                  and nowhere new to put it.
                </p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="sentinel" aria-hidden="true">↳</span>
              <div>
                <h3>Atoms sorts out yesterday</h3>
                <p>
                  It reads past days and gives each thought its own note, with a
                  real title and links to what it relates to.
                </p>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="sentinel" aria-hidden="true">↳</span>
              <div>
                <h3>Now you can find it</h3>
                <p>Ask for it, or let it come back to you. Both are below.</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>

          <div class="specimen specimen--inline">
            <p class="stage">Your daily note</p>
            <div class="file">
              <pre class="file-body"><span class="verbatim">- sam says the building has no elevator and he regrets it</span>
<span class="verbatim">- pick up milk</span></pre>
            </div>

            <p class="stage">What Atoms makes</p>
            <div class="file">
              <span class="file-name"
                >Sam regrets the building with no elevator</span
              >
              <pre class="file-body"><span class="verbatim">sam says the building has no elevator and he regrets it</span>

Linked to <span class="wl">Sam</span> and <span class="wl">Apartment hunting</span>.</pre>
            </div>

            <p class="caption">
              Your original line is never touched. The text is copied across
              word for word, and the milk stays milk.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Recall: pull -->
      <section class="band" id="ask">
        <div class="wrap">
          <p class="eyebrow">When you go looking</p>
          <h2>Ask from Claude or ChatGPT</h2>
          <p>
            Atoms plugs into the chat window you already have open, so your own
            notes become something you can question.
          </p>

          <ul class="facts">
            <li>
              <strong>It reads the library, not the pile.</strong> Every note it
              looks at is one Atoms already made: real title, tags, and links to
              what it relates to. That is why the answers are any good. Pointing
              a chatbot at a folder of raw daily pages does not work, and this
              is the difference.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Ask for it.</strong> It finds your notes by title, tags,
              and text, then quotes them back with a link to the original.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Follow the thread.</strong> Ask what connects to something
              and it walks the links between your notes.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Add without leaving chat.</strong> Tell it to remember
              something and it queues a new note for your vault. It lands next
              time Obsidian is open.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Change your mind safely.</strong> A revision becomes a new
              note linked to the old one. It never overwrites you.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <p class="fineprint">
            Matching is on the words you actually wrote, not a semantic model.
            Your daily notes and the rest of your vault are never sent, only the
            notes Atoms filed. Connector URL for Plus:
            <span class="mono">https://plus.tryatoms.app/mcp</span>
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Recall: push -->
      <section class="band" id="resurface">
        <div class="wrap">
          <p class="eyebrow">When you are not looking</p>
          <h2>Sometimes it finds you</h2>
          <p>Open Atoms and it may hand you one thing you had forgotten.</p>

          <ul class="facts">
            <li>
              <!-- Placeholder name only. Never ship a real person from a vault. -->
              <strong>Also about Sam.</strong> Write something new about someone
              and an older note about them comes back.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>On this day.</strong> Something you wrote on this date a
              year ago.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>One card, then done.</strong> Tap to open it, or ask for
              another. The same memory will not return for a week.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <p class="fineprint fineprint--legible">
            Only while you have Atoms open. No notifications, no reminders, no
            review queue, and nothing is ever due. If you do not open Atoms,
            nothing happens.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Trust -->
      <section class="band">
        <div class="wrap">
          <p class="eyebrow">What stays true</p>

          <ul class="facts">
            <li>
              <strong>Your words, unchanged.</strong> Only the title, tags, and
              links are written for you.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Links, not folders.</strong> Nothing gets filed away
              somewhere you have to remember.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Plain files you own.</strong> Uninstall tomorrow and every
              note is still there, still readable.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Not a task app.</strong> No due dates, no checklists, no
              backlog filling up behind you.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Pricing -->
      <section class="band" id="pricing">
        <div class="wrap">
          <p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p>
          <h2>${{monthlyUsd}} a month, or free with your own key.</h2>

          <div class="cards-2">
            <div class="card card--plus">
              <h3>Atoms Plus</h3>
              <p class="price">
                <span class="amount">${{monthlyUsd}}</span>
                <span class="period">per month</span>
              </p>
              <p class="alt">
                ${{yearlyUsd}} per year · {{yearlyDiscountNote}}
              </p>
              <p>
                No API key to set up, on any device. Asking from Claude and
                ChatGPT is included. {{trialDays}} day free trial.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card">
              <h3>Your Own Key</h3>
              <p class="price">
                <span class="amount">Free</span>
                <span class="period">forever</span>
              </p>
              <p class="alt">You pay Anthropic directly for usage.</p>
              <p>
                Add your Anthropic API key in Settings and Atoms works. Asking
                from chat is hosted, so it is Plus, or self host it yourself.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p class="fineprint fineprint--legible">
            Plus includes {{includedFilingsPerPeriod}} notes filed each month.
            Unused ones do not roll over. Extra filings are ${{topUpUsd}} for
            {{topUpFilings}}, one time. {{trialFinePrint}} You cancel from
            Settings inside the plugin. Prices in USD.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Install -->
      <section class="band" id="install">
        <div class="wrap">
          <p class="eyebrow">Install</p>
          <h2>Get Atoms</h2>
          <p>Atoms is not in the plugin directory yet, so it goes through BRAT.</p>

          <ol class="install">
            <li>
              Install
              <a href="https://obsidian.md/plugins?id=obsidian42-brat">BRAT</a>
              from Obsidian's community plugins.
            </li>
            <li>
              Add the beta plugin
              <span class="mono">taihartman/obsidian-atoms</span>.
            </li>
            <li>Enable <strong>Atoms</strong>.</li>
            <li>
              Open <strong>Settings → Atoms</strong> and add your key, or start
              a trial.
            </li>
          </ol>

          <p class="fineprint">
            Rather read the code first? It is all on
            <a href="https://github.com/taihartman/obsidian-atoms">GitHub</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Privacy -->
      <section class="band" id="privacy-summary">
        <div class="wrap">
          <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
          <h2>Where your notes go</h2>

          <ul class="facts">
            <li>
              <strong>Processing sends capture text to Anthropic.</strong> That
              is how the sorting works. On Plus it goes under our account, on
              your own key it goes under yours.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>We do not train on your notes.</strong>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Asking from chat is opt in.</strong> Nothing leaves your
              vault until you turn it on, and then only your atoms folder. It
              goes one direction only, and never writes back over a note.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <p class="fineprint">
            The whole story is on the <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a> page.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="foot">
      <div class="wrap">
        <nav>
          <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
          <a href="/terms">Terms</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/taihartman/obsidian-atoms">GitHub</a>
          <!--
            Support goes to GitHub Issues because no support mailbox exists yet.
            Resend on mail.tryatoms.app is send-only. If a real inbox is set up,
            swap this for a mailto: and update privacy.html + terms.html too.
          -->
          <a href="https://github.com/taihartman/obsidian-atoms/issues"
            >Support</a
          >
        </nav>
        <p style="margin: 0">
          Atoms is an independent Obsidian plugin. Obsidian is a trademark of
          Dynalist Inc., which is not affiliated with this project.
        </p>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
